# Build check and push to main

After finishing any implementation, fix, or meaningful code change in this repo:

1. Run the monorepo build check: `npm run build` from the repo root.
2. If the build fails, fix the failure and re-run the build until it passes.
3. Commit the relevant changes (do not commit secrets such as `.env`).
4. Push to the GitHub `main` branch (`git push origin main`). Work on `main` unless the user asks for a different branch.

Do this as part of completing the task — do not wait for a separate “please push” message when the user has already set this standing preference.
